<title>FINLAND: RAISIO LOOKING INTO MONSANTO PLAN.</title>
<headline>RAISIO LOOKING INTO MONSANTO PLAN.</headline>
<dateline>HELSINKI 1997-07-31</dateline>
<text>
<p>Finnish food, animal feed and chemicals group Raisio said on Thursday it was looking into a plan by Monsanto Co to develop cholesterol-cutting food products, but had no immediate comment.</p>
<p>Spokesman Sten von Hellens said he was consulting company experts on the plan, and would comment later.</p>
<p>The new product, which Monsanto said on Wednesday could take between two and 10 years to bring to market, could rival Raisio's Benecol fat-soluble cholesterol-cutting agent, which it plans to launch in the U.S. with Johnson &amp; Johnson .</p>
<p>Raisio's stock fell sharply in thin early trade on the report.</p>
